  "source_findings": [
    "Both matched historical and newest vanilla backends pass the full growing sequence to model.model(...,cache=None) at every generated token. The final hidden state is projected once; the head is already optimized.",
    "Installed mlx-lm0.28.3 Qwen3 accepts one standard KVCache per28 layers. Attention offsets RoPE by cache.offset and calls update_and_fetch; model.layers is exposed. The existing legacy beam decoder already uses this API.",
    "Both loaders explicitly require Apple Metal and set mx.gpu; there is no CPU inference fallback. Low CPU/RSS process observations alone do not measure Metal utilization.",
    "Provider timing includes prompt/tokenizer/mask/forward/strict postflight; no per-forward device timer exists, so recorded timings cannot isolate GPU cost from all provider overhead.",
    "Native prefix replay and other outside-provider case work account for at most0.482% of historical time and0.700% of newest first-case time. Historical cases did not prove, so these data do not measure successful fresh-process independent replay cost.",
    "LoRA matrices remain exactfloat32 with existing LoRALinear casts back to activationdtype; proposed caching does not change adapter precision, activation precision, quantization, authority or proof checking."
  ],
  "implementation_plan": [
    "Use proposed PerTacticKVBackend as a separately versioned backend only after current sealed comparison finishes. Construct a fresh instance for EACH new CandidatePolicy.propose; pass existing authenticated model/mx/kind and actual limits; close in finally.",
    "Prefill the complete exact prompt once, retain28 non-rotating/unquantized layer caches, then feed only the last emitted token. Require every full sequence argument to be the exact prior sequence plus that token. Never share across tactics/goals/models/requests.",
    "Keep greedy argmax, lowest-token-id tie handling, legacy-only authority mask, trained prompt/EOS parser, current no-imports validator,128token cap/6144context/30s provider/300s search/360s worker limits and independent native replay unchanged.",
    "Keep one actual forward/completion and token charge per decision. Add explicit prefill/incremental token positions and actual allocated KV bytes; no model-call discounts.",
    "Expected maximum allocated K/V is672MiB with2-byte activations or1344MiB with4-byte activations at6144tokens, plus model/temporary arrays; existing6GiBMLX and8GiBworker limits remain. Do not raise limits silently."
  ],
  "validation_needed_before_activation": [
    "AST-only currently passed; proposed code has NOT run a tensor forward and has NOT been numerically validated.",
    "CPU fake-cache unit tests should verify one prefill then single-token inputs, exact prefix/offset continuity, fresh context for every propose, exception poisoning/close, counters, masks, context/memory bounds and deadline callbacks.",
    "After current run ends, bounded serial fixed-prompt old/new-backend comparison on the same authenticated adapter: record prompt/inputIDs, logits error and top-two margins, exact greedy decisionIDs/EOS/actions, timing and peak memory. Cached and full-prefix floating-point operation shapes can differ; do not assume bitwise/token identity.",
    "Check near-tie, long-context, invalid-output and deadline cases. Keep fresh native replay authoritative regardless of decoder differences.",
    "If numerical or token differences occur, label it a new runtime and rerun a small precommitted fair panel for both compared adapters; do not append cached cases to the current frozen full-prefix arm."
  ],
